# A 64 KB data cache on the ESP32-S3 (planning/ac4.md, D14g), on top of sdkconfig.s3-fast. The
# S3 images that carry the AC-4 decoder are built with it (decision 43, 2026-10-11).
#
#   SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="...;sdkconfig.ac4;sdkconfig.s3-fast;sdkconfig.s3-dcache" idf.py build
#
# The decoder's working set (a channel's QMF matrix is 16 KB, an inverse transform's tables 56 KB)
# is what the 32 KB cache cannot hold, and the part's internal RAM is what a 64 KB one is made
# from: 32 KB of the heap. An AC-4 play with Wi-Fi up and the Sendspin player idle starts with 62 KB
# free instead of 95 and its least was 31 to 49 KB instead of 64 to 81. What it buys, with the
# second lane on (an AC-4 frame's time against its duration):
#
#                     s3-fast   + this
#   2.0 A-SPX            0.61     0.50
#   5.1 SIMPLE           1.17     0.99
#   5.1 A-SPX            1.49     1.25
#   5.1 A-CPL mode 3     1.93     1.57
#   5.1.4 S-CPL          2.67     2.28
#   29.97 fps converter  1.13     0.87
#
# Wi-Fi and lwIP cannot live on a few kilobytes (planning/ac4.md, D14c); the owner decided on
# 2026-10-11 to spend that headroom (decision 43), and this stays a separate file so that a
# build that needs the 32 KB back drops one line.
CONFIG_ESP32S3_DATA_CACHE_64KB=y

# Not for an image without the AC-4 decoder (the S3 board's release image). Measured on
# 2026-10-11 on the release shape with this file: 31,871 bytes of internal RAM free at a play's
# start, no room for the decode task's 32 KB stack, and with the stack in PSRAM 1,479 bytes free
# at the least in an E-AC-3 7.1.4 play; and the cache bought AC-3 and E-AC-3 nothing (5.1 at
# 0.32 and 0.33 of a frame without it, 0.29 and 0.33 with it; 7.1.4 at 0.75 either way).
